# Legal pages stay current

Fan-site stubs live at:

| Page | Path |
|---|---|
| About + non-affiliation | `legal/about/index.html` |
| Terms of Service | `legal/terms/index.html` |
| Privacy (+ history.db) | `legal/privacy/index.html` |
| Footer disclaimer / links | `js/shared/footer.js` (+ styles in `css/shared.css`) |

These are **stubs, not lawyer-reviewed**. Still update them when the site’s real behavior changes so they don’t lie.

## When you must update (if the change ships)

Update the matching page(s) in the **same task** (or call it out if the user deferred legal copy):

| Change | Touch |
|---|---|
| Auth / accounts / email / Steam–Discord login | Privacy (+ Terms conduct / accounts) |
| Ads, analytics, page-view counts, affiliates, paid membership, Stripe | Privacy + Terms; leave Monetization/IP research honest |
| Screenshot import: where the image is read, stored, or sent | Privacy screenshot section + Terms screenshot blurb |
| Votes bound to profiles, captcha, rate limits | Privacy (votes) |
| history.db: new fields stored, retention, delete UX, upload prompts | Privacy history section; Terms history blurb if needed |
| UGC rules, OP approval, moderation, soft-hide, bans | Terms |
| Public claims of affiliation, official status, or publisher partnership | About + footer disclaimer |
| New public contact channel for privacy/deletion requests | Privacy + Terms contact |
| Footer link set or disclaimer wording | `js/shared/footer.js` (full + slim variants) |

## Habits

- Do this in the **same task** as the behavior change. Set each touched page’s “Last updated” date
- These pages use the rewards plate (`.bpb-panel--rewards`) on the town scene. Titles are gold uppercase Baskerville. Do not put them back on parchment, Milonga sticker titles, or cream outlines
- Prefer small, accurate stub edits over long new essays
- Keep the “not legal advice / may change” note
- Do **not** invent a specific publisher legal entity name — “developers and publishers of Backpack Battles” is enough
- Do **not** mark Monetization + IP risk “done” just because stubs exist — that stays a separate research todo
- Create/admin stay footer-less unless the user asks otherwise
